// A column counts code points, not bytes, so `line:col` lands on `nope`
// even though the same line holds an accent, an arrow and an emoji before
// it. Counting bytes put this error at column 25 -- four past the end of the
// name, with the caret inside `);`. The caret's own padding is display width
// rather than the column count -- see 1046 to 1049 -- so the wide emoji
// pushes it one cell further right than the column number alone would.
print("héllo → 🎉" + nope);
